# linux-meson-s7d-current.config
#
# Kernel .config for ODROID-C5 / Amlogic S7D (S905X5M) BSP — Track A
#
# CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# This file MUST be a COMPLETE, VALIDATED Linux kernel .config file copied from:
#   • A successful first Armbian build WITH KERNEL_CONFIGURE=yes, OR
#   • Extracted directly from Hardkernel's BSP defconfig
#     (location: DannieDarko/odroid-c5_linux.git (common_drivers submodule) → arch/arm64/configs/odroidc5_defconfig or equivalent)
#
# Do NOT hand-edit this file as a fragment or partial config. This file overrides the ENTIRE kernel .config.
# If you provide an incomplete stub, the build will succeed with wrong symbols, and kernel will fail at runtime.
#
# Workflow:
#   1. First build: ./compile.sh build BOARD=odroidc5 BRANCH=current RELEASE=noble KERNEL_CONFIGURE=yes
#   2. At interactive menuconfig: exit without changes (or make board-specific tweaks)
#   3. After build: cp cache/sources/linux-*/arch/arm64/configs/.config  config/kernel/linux-meson-s7d-current.config
#   4. Commit config alongside kernel patches.
#
# See: armbian-board-patches SKILL section 6 (Kernel .config changes are NOT patches)
